# The Suave standard library

This page is written by `tools/gen-docs.js` from the real modules. Run `suave doc std.json` for any module, and use one with `use std.json`.
**61 modules, 1174 functions.**


## Data formats

### std.json

Read and write JSON, with exact line and column errors, a lenient mode (comments, trailing commas), JSON Lines and big integers.

`use std.json`  (11 things)

Functions: `compact`, `minify`, `parse`, `parse_lines`, `pretty`, `read`, `stringify`, `stringify_lines`, `try_parse`, `valid`, `write`

### std.yaml

YAML 1.2: block and flow collections, quoted, plain and block text, anchors, merge keys and several documents.

`use std.yaml`  (8 things)

Functions: `parse`, `parse_all`, `pretty`, `read`, `stringify`, `try_parse`, `valid`, `write`

### std.toml

TOML 1.0: tables, arrays of tables, dotted keys, inline tables, every string kind and dates.

`use std.toml`  (7 things)

Functions: `parse`, `pretty`, `read`, `stringify`, `try_parse`, `valid`, `write`

### std.suvl

Suave's own data format: friendly like YAML, exact like JSON, typed like TOML (durations, sizes, dates). See docs/SUVL.md.

`use std.suvl`  (8 things)

Functions: `parse`, `parse_raw`, `pretty`, `read`, `stringify`, `try_parse`, `valid`, `write`

### std.csv

CSV and TSV with quoted fields, headers into maps and optional type guessing.

`use std.csv`  (9 things)

Values: `tsv`

Functions: `parse`, `parse_rows`, `pretty`, `read`, `stringify`, `try_parse`, `valid`, `write`

### std.data

Change between formats (json, yaml, toml, suvl, csv), load and save files by their extension, guess a format.

`use std.data`  (7 things)

Functions: `convert`, `detect`, `formats`, `load`, `parse`, `save`, `stringify`

### std.xml

Parse and write XML, find tags, follow paths, turn a tree into a map.

`use std.xml`  (12 things)

Functions: `attr`, `element`, `escape`, `find`, `find_all`, `parse`, `read`, `select`, `stringify`, `text_of`, `to_map`, `unescape`

### std.ini

INI and config files.

`use std.ini`  (3 things)

Functions: `parse`, `read`, `stringify`

### std.table

Data frames: filter, sort, group, join, summarize and print tables of rows. Reads CSV.

`use std.table`  (6 things)

Functions: `from`, `from_columns`, `from_csv`, `new`, `read_csv`, `write_csv`

